{"name":"Origami","hex":"#ece0c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"origami","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The Japanese art of paper folding.","A piece of art made by folding paper."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To construct by means of decorative paper folding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/origami"}],"entries":[{"title":"Origami","blocks":[{"text":"Origami  is the art and technique of folding paper. It also refers to the two- and three-dimensional forms created in the process. The use of the term has been extended in modern times to include other materials such as metal, textiles, and it is also used in the biological sciences to describe folded structures like DNA."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cranes_made_by_Origami_paper.jpg/330px-Cranes_made_by_Origami_paper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origami","wikidata":"Q83357"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Hiroshima_senzaburu.jpg/500px-Hiroshima_senzaburu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Hiroshima_senzaburu.jpg/500px-Hiroshima_senzaburu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A group of Japanese schoolchildren dedicate their contribution of senbazuru at the Sadako Sasaki\nmemorial in Hiroshima.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHiroshima_senzaburu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Hiden_Senbazuru_Orikata.jpg/500px-Hiden_Senbazuru_Orikata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Hiden_Senbazuru_Orikata.jpg/1280px-Hiden_Senbazuru_Orikata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu